module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AffineBaseCoveringSieveStepOne
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.PointSetCoverLocallySurjective
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Size.FlatAtlasOpenSubspace
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The chart tools of Stacks 02W8 for a flat chart

Steps 2 to 5 of the proof of Stacks 02W8 are carried out in this library for a chart of the
descended sheaf which is *surjective étale* after every represented base change, because that is
the chart a descent datum along a surjective étale morphism of the big fppf site of `S` provides.
A descent problem along a *covering sieve* over an affine base provides a chart as well, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.coveringSieveBody_affineBase_of_affineFlatSource`, but a flat one: the
single morphism that step 1 of Descent, Lemma 02W3 produces is surjective, flat, locally of
finite presentation and quasi-compact, with no étaleness.

This file records that each of the four chart tools those steps consume works for a flat chart,
with the same proof.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presheafIsOpenMap_of_isPullback_of_flat`: the openness input of step 2
  — a chart presented as a base change of a surjective flat morphism locally of finite
  presentation is an open map of schemes after every represented base change.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_size_bound_of_flatChart`: the uniform size bound of step 5 —
  one cardinal below the site's cutoff bounds every object of the site representing an open
  subspace of a presheaf carrying a flat chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presheaf_of_surjectiveFlatChart_of_descendsAlong`: the property half
  of Stacks 03I2 for a flat chart, with no descent hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_flat_isPullback_presheaf_of_chart` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presheaf_of_surjectiveFlatChart_of_coveringSieveDescent`: the
  representability half of Stacks 03I2 for a flat chart, from effective descent along the
  *covering sieves* of the site. The covering sieve used is the one generated by the base change
  of the chart, which is a covering sieve precisely because a surjective flat morphism locally of
  finite presentation is a one-element fppf covering.

## Implementation notes

*Why the étale statements survive unchanged.* Étaleness is consumed in exactly two ways by the
chart tools. Either it is turned into flatness together with local finite presentation —
`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.iff_flat_and_formallyUnramified` — and used through
`AlgebraicGeometry.UniversallyOpen.of_flat` (Stacks 01UA), through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.size_le_of_flat_of_surjective`, or through the fppf descent of a
property; or it is used to make a single morphism into a one-element covering of the site, which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.singleton_mem_fppfPrecoverage` does for a surjective flat morphism
locally of finite presentation just as well. Neither use needs unramifiedness, so every statement
below is the étale one with `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale` replaced by the pair
`AlgebraicGeometry.Flat`, `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFinitePresentation`. The étale statements
are kept: they are what the surjective-étale descent predicate consumes.

*Why the representability half changes shape and the property half does not.* The property half
is fppf descent of a property of an existing morphism, and a single surjective flat morphism
locally of finite presentation is an fppf covering of the site, so it transfers verbatim. The
representability half is effective descent, and for a flat chart the hypothesis available is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve` rather than
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsEffectiveDescentAlongSurjectiveEtale` — the latter quantifies over
étale covering morphisms and says nothing about a flat one. The covering-sieve predicate is the
strictly stronger of the two, so this is not a weakening: it is the only one of the two which
applies.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02W8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02W8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03I2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03I2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01UA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01UA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03JH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03JH)
-/

@[expose] public section

open Cardinal CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-! ### The openness input of step 2 for a flat chart -/

variable {B S hS}

/-- **The openness input of the second step of Stacks 02W8, for a flat chart.** A morphism of
presheaves on the big fppf site of `S` which is a represented base change of `yoneda.map p` for a
flat morphism `p` of the site locally of finite presentation is an open map of schemes after every
represented base change.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presheafIsOpenMap_of_isPullback_of_etale` with étaleness weakened
to flatness together with local finite presentation, which is all that
`AlgebraicGeometry.UniversallyOpen.of_flat` — Stacks 01UA — asks for. -/
@[sga "3 X 4.7" "more general"]
theorem presheafIsOpenMap_of_isPullback_of_flat
    {G : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {a c : BigFppfOver B S hS}
    {π : G ⟶ yoneda.obj a} {p : c ⟶ a} {V : BigFppfOver B S hS} {g : yoneda.obj V ⟶ G}
    {ρ : yoneda.obj V ⟶ yoneda.obj c} (sq : IsPullback g ρ π (yoneda.map p))
    (hpf : Flat ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map p))
    (hpp : LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map p)) :
    (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (topologically @IsOpenMap : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf g := by
  have _ := hpf
  have _ := hpp
  have hqo : (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.UniversallyOpen.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (yoneda.map p) :=
    (BigFppfOver.presheaf_inverseImage_yoneda_map_iff B S hS _ p).2
      (UniversallyOpen.of_flat _)
  have _ := MorphismProperty.relative_isStableUnderBaseChange (F := yoneda)
    (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.UniversallyOpen.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))
  have hle : (@_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.UniversallyOpen.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) ≤
      (topologically @IsOpenMap : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) := fun _ _ k hk =>
    have := hk
    k.isOpenMap
  exact MorphismProperty.relative_monotone
    (MorphismProperty.monotone_inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS) hle) _
    (MorphismProperty.of_isPullback sq.flip hqo)

/-! ### The uniform size bound of step 5 for a flat chart -/

/-- **A flat chart bounds the size of every representable open subspace of the presheaf it
charts, uniformly.** Let `g : yoneda.obj U ⟶ G` present `yoneda.obj U` as a base change of
`yoneda.map p` along a morphism `π : G ⟶ yoneda.obj a`, for a surjective flat morphism `p` of the
big fppf site of `S`. Then there is a single cardinal below the site's cutoff bounding the size
of every object `V` of the site admitting an open immersion `yoneda.obj V ⟶ G`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_size_bound_of_descentDatum` with the surjective étale
covering morphism weakened to a surjective flat one and the datum replaced by the chart it
produces. The bound is `max (2 ^ #U) (2 ^ size U)`, which mentions only `U` and lies below the
cutoff by `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.cutoff_isStrongPrelimit`; it comes from
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.size_le_of_isOpenImmersion_of_flatAtlas`, the flat form of the bound of
Tag 03JH.

Nothing is asked of `G` — not the sheaf condition, not representability — which is the point,
since its representability is what the glueing step is for. -/
theorem exists_size_bound_of_flatChart {G : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u}
    {a c : BigFppfOver B S hS} {π : G ⟶ yoneda.obj a} {p : c ⟶ a}
    (hps : Surjective ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map p))
    (hpf : Flat ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map p))
    {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} {g : yoneda.obj U ⟶ G} {ρ : yoneda.obj U ⟶ yoneda.obj c}
    (sq : IsPullback g ρ π (yoneda.map p)) :
    ∃ μ : Cardinal.{u}, μ < B.cutoff ∧ ∀ (V : BigFppfOver B S hS)
      (k : yoneda.obj V ⟶ G), IsOpenImmersion B S hS k →
        ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V).size ≤ μ := by
  have hps' : (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (yoneda.map p) :=
    (BigFppfOver.presheaf_inverseImage_yoneda_map_iff B S hS _ p).2 hps
  have hpf' : (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Flat.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (yoneda.map p) :=
    (BigFppfOver.presheaf_inverseImage_yoneda_map_iff B S hS _ p).2 hpf
  have _ := MorphismProperty.relative_isStableUnderBaseChange (F := yoneda)
    (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))
  have _ := MorphismProperty.relative_isStableUnderBaseChange (F := yoneda)
    (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Flat.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))
  refine ⟨max (2 ^ #((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U : Type u))
      (2 ^ ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U).size),
    Scheme.max_two_pow_mk_two_pow_size_lt_of_isStrongPrelimit B.cutoff_isStrongPrelimit
      U.left.property, fun V k hk => ?_⟩
  exact size_le_of_isOpenImmersion_of_flatAtlas B S hS
    (MorphismProperty.of_isPullback sq.flip hps')
    (MorphismProperty.of_isPullback sq.flip hpf') hk

/-! ### The property half of Stacks 03I2 for a flat chart -/

/-- **The property half of Stacks 03I2 for a flat chart, unconditionally.** Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a
*representable* morphism of presheaves on the big fppf site of `S`, let `g : yoneda.obj U ⟶ Y` be
a chart of its target which is surjective, flat and locally of finite presentation after every
represented base change, and let `r` be a base change of `f` along `g`. If `r` is representable
with a property `Q` of morphisms of schemes which descends along the surjective flat morphisms of
finite presentation, then `f` itself is representable with `Q`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presheaf_of_surjectiveEtaleChart_of_descendsAlong` with étaleness
of the chart weakened to flatness together with local finite presentation: that theorem consumes
étaleness only by turning it into the conjunction `surjective ⊓ flat ⊓ locally of finite
presentation` which Mathlib's fppf descent asks for, and the conjunction is now a hypothesis. No
effective descent is needed, the representability of `f` being assumed. -/
theorem presheaf_of_surjectiveFlatChart_of_descendsAlong
    {Q : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}} [Q.RespectsIso]
    [Q.DescendsAlong (@Surjective ⊓ @Flat ⊓ @LocallyOfFinitePresentation)]
    {X Y : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {f : X ⟶ Y}
    (hf : yoneda.relativelyRepresentable f)
    {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} {g : yoneda.obj U ⟶ Y}
    (hs : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) g)
    (hfl : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Flat.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) g)
    (hfp : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@LocallyOfFinitePresentation.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) g)
    {A : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {m : A ⟶ X} {r : A ⟶ yoneda.obj U}
    (sq : IsPullback m r f g)
    (hr : (Q.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf r) :
    (Q.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf f := by
  have : MorphismProperty.RespectsIso (Q.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)) :=
    MorphismProperty.RespectsIso.inverseImage _ _
  refine MorphismProperty.relative_of_snd hf fun a k ↦ ?_
  have hwsq : IsPullback (hs.rep.fst k) (yoneda.map (hs.rep.snd k)) g k := hs.rep.isPullback k
  have hwsurj : Surjective ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hs.rep.snd k)) :=
    hs.property_snd k
  have hwflat : Flat ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hs.rep.snd k)) :=
    hfl.property k (hs.rep.fst k) (hs.rep.snd k) hwsq
  have hwlfp : LocallyOfFinitePresentation
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hs.rep.snd k)) :=
    hfp.property k (hs.rep.fst k) (hs.rep.snd k) hwsq
  have pbC : IsPullback (pullback.fst (hf.snd k) (hs.rep.snd k))
      (pullback.snd (hf.snd k) (hs.rep.snd k)) (hf.snd k) (hs.rep.snd k) :=
    IsPullback.of_hasPullback _ _
  have hbig : IsPullback (yoneda.map (pullback.fst (hf.snd k) (hs.rep.snd k)) ≫ hf.fst k)
      (yoneda.map (pullback.snd (hf.snd k) (hs.rep.snd k))) f
      (hs.rep.fst k ≫ g) := by
    rw [hwsq.w]
    exact (pbC.map yoneda).paste_horiz (hf.isPullback k)
  exact MorphismProperty.of_isPullback_of_descendsAlong
    (Q := (@Surjective ⊓ @Flat ⊓ @LocallyOfFinitePresentation : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}))
    (pbC.map (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).flip ⟨⟨hwsurj, hwflat⟩, hwlfp⟩
    (hr.property (hs.rep.fst k) _ _ (hbig.of_right' sq))

/-! ### The representability half of Stacks 03I2 for a flat chart -/

/-- A surjective flat chart locally of finite presentation along which the base change of `f`
satisfies the presheaf property attached to `P` produces, over every representable base change of
`f`, a surjective flat morphism of the site locally of finite presentation after which that base
change again satisfies the property.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_etale_isPullback_presheaf_of_chart` with étaleness
weakened to flatness together with local finite presentation. Unlike the étale statement it
records only the base-changed morphism and the property of the base change along it, rather than
the descent datum: the covering-sieve predicate consumes exactly that. -/
theorem exists_flat_isPullback_presheaf_of_chart {P : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}}
    [P.RespectsIso] {X Y : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {f : X ⟶ Y}
    {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} {g : yoneda.obj U ⟶ Y}
    (hs : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) g)
    (hfl : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Flat.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) g)
    (hfp : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@LocallyOfFinitePresentation.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) g)
    (hV : (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (pullback.snd f g))
    (a : BigFppfOver B S hS) (h : yoneda.obj a ⟶ Y) :
    ∃ (c : BigFppfOver B S hS) (q : c ⟶ a),
      Surjective ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map q) ∧
      Flat ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map q) ∧
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map q) ∧
      (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf
        (pullback.snd f (yoneda.map q ≫ h)) := by
  have hbc := MorphismProperty.relative_isStableUnderBaseChange (F := yoneda)
    (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))
  have hri : MorphismProperty.RespectsIso
      ((P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf) := hbc.respectsIso
  have sq := hs.rep.isPullback h
  refine ⟨hs.rep.pullback h, hs.rep.snd h, hs.property h _ _ sq,
    hfl.property h _ _ sq, hfp.property h _ _ sq, ?_⟩
  have hsqR := (IsPullback.of_hasPullback f (hs.rep.fst h ≫ g)).of_right'
    (IsPullback.of_hasPullback f g)
  have key : ∀ k : yoneda.obj (hs.rep.pullback h) ⟶ Y,
      k = yoneda.map (hs.rep.snd h) ≫ h →
      (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (pullback.snd f k) →
      (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf
        (pullback.snd f (yoneda.map (hs.rep.snd h) ≫ h)) := by
    intro k hk
    subst hk
    exact id
  exact key _ sq.w (MorphismProperty.of_isPullback hsqR hV)

/-- **The representability half of Stacks 03I2 for a flat chart, from effective descent along the
covering sieves.** A morphism from a sheaf to a sheaf on the big fppf site of `S` whose base
change along one chart of its target which is surjective, flat and locally of finite presentation
after every represented base change is representable with `Q` is itself representable with `Q`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presheaf_of_surjectiveEtaleChart` for a flat chart. The
hypothesis has to be the covering-sieve predicate and not the surjective-étale one, which says
nothing about a flat covering morphism; the covering sieve used at an object `a` of the site is
the one generated by the base change `q` of the chart along the morphism `yoneda.obj a ⟶ Y` being
tested, a covering sieve by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.sieve_generate_singleton_mem_topology_over_of_flat`, and the hypothesis
of the predicate holds along its arrows `u ≫ q` because they are base changes of `q`. -/
theorem presheaf_of_surjectiveFlatChart_of_coveringSieveDescent
    {Q : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}} [Q.RespectsIso]
    (hdesc : IsEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve B S hS Q)
    {X Y : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u}
    (hX : Presheaf.IsSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) X)
    (hY : Presheaf.IsSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) Y) {f : X ⟶ Y}
    {U : BigFppfOver B S hS} {g : yoneda.obj U ⟶ Y}
    (hs : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) g)
    (hfl : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Flat.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) g)
    (hfp : (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@LocallyOfFinitePresentation.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))) g)
    (hV : (Q.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (pullback.snd f g)) :
    (Q.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf f := by
  have hbc := MorphismProperty.relative_isStableUnderBaseChange (F := yoneda)
    (Q.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS))
  have hri : MorphismProperty.RespectsIso
      (Q.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)) :=
    MorphismProperty.RespectsIso.inverseImage _ _
  refine (MorphismProperty.presheaf_iff_forall_presheaf_pullback_snd _ f).2 fun a h ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨c, q, hqs, hqf, hqp, hQ⟩ :=
    exists_flat_isPullback_presheaf_of_chart hs hfl hfp hV a h
  refine hdesc f hX hY h _
    (sieve_generate_singleton_mem_topology_over_of_flat B S hS q hqs hqf hqp) ?_
  rintro b k ⟨Z, u, w, hw, hfac⟩
  cases hw
  have hsqR := (IsPullback.of_hasPullback f (yoneda.map u ≫ yoneda.map q ≫ h)).of_right'
    (IsPullback.of_hasPullback f (yoneda.map q ≫ h))
  have key : ∀ l : yoneda.obj b ⟶ Y, l = yoneda.map k ≫ h →
      (Q.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (pullback.snd f l) →
      (Q.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf
        (pullback.snd f (yoneda.map k ≫ h)) := by
    intro l hl
    subst hl
    exact id
  refine key _ ?_ (MorphismProperty.of_isPullback hsqR hQ)
  rw [← hfac, Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc]

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
